FINDINGS: #C642 ff32f14. The rebase is clean (range-diff: only CHANGELOG context and the merged OWNER_ENTRIES, which holds both gate/publish.mjs and collector/collect.mjs), and the isDeletion change is right for cards, threads and plan. But with gate.requireUpdatedAt true (which the pack sets), updatedAt is required on every set/update of the five stamped collections, and two allow lists refuse it. Probed with checkWrites, lead and Ops, config gate.requireUpdatedAt true:
1. HIGH, gate/rules.mjs:418 (and 413): an answered ask can no longer be changed by anyone, the lead included. Close {done, doneAt, updatedAt}: refused "its wording is frozen". Reopen {response: __delete__, updatedAt}: refused. Tombstone {deleted, updatedAt}: refused. Plain delete: refused at :109 ("update it with {deleted: true...}"). Converting an answer to a decision: refused at :415 ("not updatedAt"). Without the flag, close, reopen and convert all pass. Fix: allow updatedAt in both lists, and deleted: true for the lead (keeping :419's "only the lead deletes an answered ask" for a tombstone via isDeletion).
2. HIGH, gate/plan.mjs:10/24: FIELDS lacks updatedAt, so a plan update with updatedAt is refused as an unknown field, and one without it is refused by updatedAtErrors: no plan write can pass. Fix: add updatedAt to FIELDS.
Tests: each of the above with requireUpdatedAt true (close/reopen/convert/tombstone of an answered ask by the lead allowed, tombstone by Ops refused; a plan update with updatedAt allowed), and a mutation check.
